      "type": "text", "title": "Measured baselines (offline reference, not live Prometheus)", "id": 29,
      "description": "Source: docs/benchmarks.md, updated 2026-07-24.",
      "datasource": { "type": "datasource", "uid": "grafana" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 70 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "These are **test-run baselines**, not dashboard samples or SLOs. Compare live queue, throughput, saturation, errors, and readiness against the workload shape.\n\n| Scenario | Measured result |\n|---|---:|\n| Hot create, fleet E2E (commit `06f5c16`) | 478 ms p50 / 509 ms p90 |\n| 64 concurrent creates + workload | 1.28 s p50 / 2.0 s p95; 0 failures |\n| Churn 200 @ concurrency 96 | 7.9 creates/s; create p50 5.2 s |\n| Held autoscale burst 160 from 2×48 | 8.38 s p50 / 49.82 s p99; 160/160 |\n| Held burst scale decision | 9.8 s |\n| Held burst complete | 50.02 s |\n| Snapshot restore | 84 ms p50 (current fleet rerun) |\n\nSee `docs/benchmarks.md` for clocks, environment, caveats, and the known hibernate/wake clock regression."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "title": "What is live now—and what is still missing", "id": 30,
      "datasource": { "type": "datasource", "uid": "grafana" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 70 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Live now:** 10s gateway occupancy, allocatable slots, queue depth, rejected demand, create rate, desired workers, direct scale-out attempts/failures, and release-gate mismatches; 30s per-worker pools, memory admission, create concurrency, lifecycle counters, readiness phases, process uptime, golden state, scrape health, and release identity.\n\n**Not currently emitted:** request-duration histograms (create/wake/restore p50/p95/p99), Nomad autoscaler action/confirmation timestamps, GCE MIG target/current state, host CPU/disk/network pressure, or deploy annotations.\n\nThat distinction is intentional: latency numbers above remain benchmark evidence until the HTTP paths expose histograms. For a production rollout, watch expected/observed release presence together with queue, rejection/error rates, golden readiness, direct-scaler failures, and worker readiness; do not infer live latency from the static benchmark table."
      }
    }
